#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# digit_sum

#% text
# `digit_sum(n)` gives the sum of the decimal digits of `|n|`, `digit_sum(n, b)` of its digits in base `b`. `digit_sum(n, b, k)` sums the first `k` digits (the last `-k` for negative `k`). A list of numbers or of bases gives a list.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
digit_sum(58127)
#% output
#= 23

#% cell
digit_sum(58127, 2)
#% output
#= 9

#% cell
digit_sum(6345354, 10, -4)
#% output
#= 17

#% cell
digit_sum(9^1000 + 1)
#% output
#= 4339

#% cell
digit_sum(7, [2, 3, 4])
#% output
#= [3, 3, 4]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `digit_count`, `integer_digits`, `total`
